    "title": "Police: Meridian man arrested after pointing gun at skateboarders at The Village - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By IDAHO PRESS STAFF ,\n22 hours ago\nA Meridian man was arrested Tuesday for allegedly pointing a gun at three people in The Village parking lot.\nWayne Gaddis, 44, has been charged with three counts of felony aggravated assault after, police say, he confronted three victims in their 20s who were skateboarding in The Village parking lot and pointed a 9mm handgun at them, according to a news release from the Meridian Police Department.\nOfficers responded to the scene at 12:30 a.m., after the victims left the area and called 911.\nWhile attempting to get Gaddis to surrender near Blaze Pizza, a Meridian police officer fired one round from his AR-15, the release said. The round missed Gaddis, and he was arrested without further incident. Police recovered the handgun, which was loaded with a round in the chamber.\nNeither Gaddis nor the officer who fired his gun were injured, the release said.\nGaddis was arraigned Tuesday and is being held at the Ada County Jail on a $250,000 bond, online court records show.\nThe Ada County Critical Incident Task Force (CITF), led by the Ada County Sheriff’s Office, is investigating the incident.",
